=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/trips/pages/TripReplayPage.tsx, 639 lines) replays one
drive threaded through a single source of truth — the playhead index from
`useTripReplay` — across a map, a transport scrubber, a live "current position"
stat bar, an elevation profile, a speed+power timeline, and the drive summary.
Data source: `useDrive → GET /drives/{id}`. SI display contract: position-derived
fields (speed/outsideTemp/ratedRange/cumulative distance) are SI canonical and
converted at the render boundary via `useUnits` / `convertXFromSI`.

Parity manifest record (42 = 16 panels + 2 charts + 4 states + 20 strings):
  panels  : GlassPanel1, Speed, Power, Battery, Elevation, Range, Temperature,
            GlassPanel8, Distance, Duration, Efficiency, Elevation-Gain,
            Elevation-Loss, Max-Speed, Avg-Speed, Battery-2
  charts  : Sparkline, ElevationProfile          (maps: 0 — no map in this unit)
  states  : loading, empty, error, success
  strings : 20 replay.* keys (all already present in Localizable.xcstrings)

PREDECESSOR / COLLISION FINDING (binding for the whole implementation):
  A complete sibling SwiftUI port already exists at
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Driving/TripReplay*  with PUBLIC symbols
  `TripReplayPage`, `TripReplayPageModel`, `TripReplayRecord`, `TripReplayMarker`,
  … and files `TripReplayPage.swift`, `TripReplayModels.swift`,
  `TripReplayPageModel.swift`, `TripReplayDerivations.swift`,
  `TripReplayRouteRegistration.swift`; `TripReplayCharts.swift` also exists under
  TeslaSync/feature-views/. Both source trees compile into the SINGLE `TeslaSync`
  module. Swift forbids (a) two same-name types and (b) two same-basename files in
  one target. Therefore this unit MUST use unique symbol names AND unique file
  basenames, or the target cannot build. This mirrors the repo's established
  auto-dedupe convention (e.g. commit aef073020 "auto-dedupe collision
  BackupConfig->SystemStatusModelsBackupConfig").
  Resolution: every type and file in this unit is `Trips…`-prefixed and the shared
  P2 tokens / P3 components / P1 Units facade / Swift-Charts wrappers are REUSED
  (DRY), not duplicated. The unit lives in the prescribed directory
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/; the main view file is TripsReplayPage.swift
  (the bare name TripReplayPage.swift is impossible alongside the committed
  Sources/Features/Driving/TripReplayPage.swift).

=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/
  TripsReplayModels.swift            value types (SI) + TripsReplayDataSource seam (useDrive)
  TripsReplayDerivations.swift       pure: merge, clock offsets, indexAtTime, timeline,
                                     elevation, sparkline, markers, elevation gain/loss, haversine
  TripsReplayPageModel.swift         @Observable model + replay transport clock (play/pause/stop/seek/speed)
  TripsReplayDisplay.swift           TripsReplayStatKind / TripsReplaySummaryKind (one named symbol per
                                     parity panel) + render-boundary formatting via Units (SI→display)
  TripsReplaySampleData.swift        Sample / Empty / Failing sources → the 4 data states
  TripsReplayControls.swift          transport (scrubber+buttons+speed menu) + speed Sparkline (chart #1)
  TripsReplayStats.swift             "Current Position Stats" GlassPanel + 6 metric cards (adaptive grid)
  TripsReplayCharts.swift            ElevationProfile (chart #2, Swift Charts) + speed/power timeline
  TripsReplaySummary.swift           "Drive Summary" GlassPanel + 8 stat cards (adaptive grid)
  TripsReplayPage.swift              adaptive scaffold + loading/empty/error/success + back-to-drive
  TripsReplayRouteRegistration.swift NavigationDestination deep-link (web /drives/:id/replay)

Design notes:
  - @Observable `TripsReplayModel` consumes a KMP-bindable data-source seam
    (`loadDrive` ← useDrive / GET /drives/{id}); the view holds no networking (ADR-004).
  - Single source of truth: `currentIndex` / `progressFraction`; every surface
    (scrubber, elevation playhead, timeline playhead, stat bar) derives from it and
    seeks back through `seekTo` (web `handleSeekToIndex`).
  - SI only on the model; conversion at the SwiftUI render boundary via `Units`
    (P1/S5) + `@Environment(\.tsUnits)` (ADR-005). Nothing non-SI stored/computed.
  - Adaptive macOS + iOS: LazyVGrid(.adaptive) stat/summary grids reflow; charts +
    scrubber take full width; `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)` is iOS-gated.
  - a11y: panel/chart accessibility labels + combine, marker `isSelected` trait,
    ≥44pt transport targets, dynamic Color.TS (light/dark), VoiceOver-safe overlays.
  - Data source is a one-shot fetch (not a live SSE stream) — web parity has no live
    subscription, so no >2-min staleness indicator is required for this unit.

